WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.970
- [Instructor] We're told
that we want to factor

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.400
the following expression
that they have right here

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.800
and they say that we can
factor the expression

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.650
as U plus V squared

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.500
where U and V are either constant integers

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.860
or single variable expressions.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.100
What are U and V?

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.400
And then they ask us to
actually factor the expression.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.783
So pause this video and see
if you can work on that.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.750
All right, so let's go
with the first part of it.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.280
So they say they can factor the expression

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.340
as U plus V squared.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.700
So how do we see this expression in terms

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.970
of U plus V squared?

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.040
Well one way is to just remind ourselves

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.300
what U plus V squared even is.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.310
U plus V squared, this
is just going to be a,

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.440
the square of a binomial
and you've seen this

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.300
in many, many other videos.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.440
This is going to be U
squared plus two times

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.950
the product of these two terms.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:55.240
So 2UV plus V squared.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.610
If you've never seen this before

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.180
or not sure where this
came from, I encourage you

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.660
to watch some of those early videos

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.120
where we explain this out.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.150
But, does this match this pattern?

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:10.790
Well can we express
this term as U squared?

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.590
Well if this is U
squared, then U would have

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.730
to be equal to X plus seven

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.040
and when I say, actually I
should be a little careful.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.940
Can we express this entire
thing right over here

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.640
as U squared?

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.495
If U squared is equal
to X plus seven squared,

00:01:25.495 --> 00:01:30.020
that means that U is going
to be equal to X plus seven

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.190
and then this right over here

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.210
would have to be V squared.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.110
If this is V squared,
then that means that V

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.130
is equal to Y squared
because Y squared squared

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.850
is equal to Y to the fourth.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.010
So V is equal to Y squared.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.040
Now they already told us that this,

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.080
this could be factored as the
expression U plus V squared,

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.850
but let's make sure that
this actually works.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.860
Is this middle term right over here,

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:59.860
is this truly equal to
two times U times V, 2UV?

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:01.843
Well let's see.

00:02:01.843 --> 00:02:06.570
Two times U would be
two times X plus seven

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.570
times V times Y squared

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:11.860
and that's exactly what
we have right over here.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.470
It's 2Y squared times X plus seven.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:18.150
So this kind of hairy looking expression

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.250
actually does fit this
pattern right over here.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.890
So you can view it as U plus V squared

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.750
where U is equal to X plus seven

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.020
and V is equal to Y squared.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.790
Now using that, we can now
actually factor the expression.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:35.640
We can write this thing as being equal

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.320
to U plus V squared.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.290
And we know what U and V are.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.920
So this is, this whole expression

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.920
is going to be equal to
U, which is X plus seven,

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.580
and I'll put it in
parentheses just so you see it

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.470
very clearly, plus V
plus Y squared squared,

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.440
'cause that's exactly
what we wrote over there.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.340
And of course, you don't have
to write these parentheses.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.100
You could rewrite this as X plus seven

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.070
plus Y squared squared.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.823
Let's do another example.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:10.170
So here, once again, we are told that

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.010
we want to factor the following expression

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.140
and they're saying that we
can factor the expression

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.660
as U plus V times U minus V

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.670
where U and V are either constant integers

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.430
or single variable expressions.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.380
So pause this video and try
to figure out what U and V are

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.100
and then actually factor the expression.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.300
All right, well let's just
remind ourselves in general

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:33.300
what U plus V times U minus V is equal to.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.990
Well, if this is unfamiliar to you,

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.330
I encourage you to watch the videos

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.090
on difference of squares.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.690
When you multiply this all out

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.960
this is going to give you
a difference of squares.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.810
U squared minus V squared.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.430
If you actually take the
trouble of multiplying this out,

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.960
you're going to see that that middle term,

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.830
that middle third term, or
the middle terms I should say,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.060
cancel out, so you're just
left with the U squared

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.960
minus the V squared.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.080
And so does this fit this pattern?

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.240
Well in order for this to be U squared

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.600
and for this to be V squared,

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.310
that means U squared
is equal to 4X squared

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.950
so that means that U
would have to be equal

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.840
to the square root of that
which would be two times X.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:17.750
Notice, U squared would be 2X
squared which is 4X squared

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.060
and then V would have to be equal

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.730
to the square root of 9Y to the sixth.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.491
With the square root of nine is three

00:04:24.491 --> 00:04:27.430
and the square of Y to
the sixth is going to be Y

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:28.770
to the third power.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:31.130
And then we could use that
to factor the expression,

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.833
'cause we could say hey,

00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:33.820
this right over here is the same thing

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.160
as U squared minus V squared,

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.540
so it's going to be equal to,

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.260
we can factor it out as, or factor it as,

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:45.260
U minus or U plus V times U minus V.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.250
So what's that going to be equal to?

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.690
So U plus V is going to
be equal to 2X plus 3Y

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.050
to the third and then U minus V

00:04:56.050 --> 00:05:00.440
is going to be equal to 2X,
which is our U right over here,

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:05.060
minus our V, minus 3Y to the third.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:05.893
So there you have it.

00:05:05.893 --> 00:05:07.250
We factored the expression.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.780
You might want to write it down here

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:12.593
but we just did it right
up there and we're done.

